    <div
      class="space-y-3 mb-8"
    >
      <p>
        The two methods measure different things. 
        <strong>
          WCAG 2
        </strong>
         compares how much light each color emits. 
        <strong>
          APCA
        </strong>
         models how readable text looks, and it weighs dark and light colors differently, so light text on a mid-tone scores higher than WCAG’s ratio suggests.
      </p>
    </div>
